WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:07.140
Fundraising software that doesn't live in your Salesforce org.

2
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.525
Lives somewhere else.

3
00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.433
Your donation platform holds the donors.

4
00:00:12.433 --> 00:00:14.812
Salesforce gets a copy overnight.

5
00:00:14.812 --> 00:00:16.975
And the two never quite agree.

6
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.877
Pledgivo removes the second system.

7
00:00:20.877 --> 00:00:21.523
One org.

8
00:00:21.523 --> 00:00:23.300
One copy of the truth.

9
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:29.043
A public donation form, backed by Stripe.

10
00:00:29.043 --> 00:00:34.900
The card is tokenised in the browser, and the gift lands as a standard Opportunity.

11
00:00:35.883 --> 00:00:43.683
Salesforce owns the schedule and charges the saved card itself — not a Stripe subscription living in another system.

12
00:00:45.383 --> 00:00:48.655
Every appeal is a standard Salesforce Campaign.

13
00:00:48.655 --> 00:00:52.483
There's no parallel fundraising object to keep in step.

14
00:00:53.483 --> 00:01:00.558
A page design themes the whole donor experience, composed from movable blocks rather than hard-coded.

15
00:01:01.783 --> 00:01:05.926
Write the story in Markdown, post updates, publish documents.

16
00:01:05.926 --> 00:01:09.458
A tab appears only when there's something behind it.

17
00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:17.350
Ticketed events with tiered pricing and real seat capacity, on the same pipeline as every other gift.

18
00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:22.475
Donors manage their own giving.

19
00:01:22.475 --> 00:01:26.750
A code in their inbox — no account, no password to reset.

20
00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:32.116
Receipts and every transactional email, branded from Settings.

21
00:01:32.116 --> 00:01:35.625
Your colours, your legal text, your postal address.

22
00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:40.206
Refund from the Opportunity, or straight from Stripe.

23
00:01:40.206 --> 00:01:44.067
An hourly reconciler makes sure both tell the same story.

24
00:01:45.317 --> 00:01:53.142
A failed recurring charge retries on your cadence, emails the donor, then cancels after the grace period you set.

25
00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:00.878
Contacts or Person Accounts, detected at install and never hard-coded.

26
00:02:00.878 --> 00:02:06.650
Every first-time donor gets a household Account, so no gift falls out of a report.

27
00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:12.559
A Settings console for everything an admin should tune without a deploy.

28
00:02:12.559 --> 00:02:16.650
Payment keys live in a Named Credential your own org builds.

29
00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:26.825
A monitor for gifts stuck between Stripe and Salesforce, diagnostic logs, and a queue for anything a donor asks a public page to do.

30
00:02:27.817 --> 00:02:29.039
And it travels.

31
00:02:29.039 --> 00:02:33.767
Two lines of HTML put a live campaign on any site you own.

32
00:02:35.117 --> 00:02:38.055
A managed package on the current API.

33
00:02:38.055 --> 00:02:40.834
Payment keys in a Named Credential.

34
00:02:40.834 --> 00:02:47.267
No public webhook endpoint to secure, and NPSP optional — detected, not required.

35
00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:48.873
Pledgivo.

36
00:02:48.873 --> 00:02:52.125
Keep your donors where your data already lives.

